Update: Disable GUI updates when running in Docker

Since the Docker container is run read-only and code updates
should be done by pulling a new image instead of mutating
the running container, this disables the GUI update button
when a Docker environment is detected (`/.dockerenv`).
It displays an appropriate message in the UI asking to
update the container image instead.

Also removed the alternative Python directly-on-host instructions
and systemd installation from README as requested by the user,
leaving Docker Compose as the primary recommended method.
